    "title": "Upper Valley Career Center unveils time capsule from 2000 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Southall ,\n2 hours ago\nPIQUA, Ohio ( WDTN ) – The Upper Valley Career Center unveiled a 25-year-old time capsule on Wednesday, Oct. 1.\nThe capsule was buried on Feb. 22, 2000, in the walkway between the main building and the administrative building. Back then, each career and tech program contributed an item, along with letters from administrators to their future successors.\nCedarville University holds annual cardboard canoe race Several staff and administrators from 2000 were present at the opening, and four Senior Landscape and Natural Resources students assisted in excavating the capsule.\nFormer superintendent Karl Wilson, prior business manager Larry Wahrer, and prior director Dr. Larry Householder unpacked the contents for the crowd.\nInside the time capsule, there were photographs, a menu from the Upper Valley Inn, and an old enrollment book.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.",
